      "text": "**Project Hail Mary** is a science fiction novel written by **Andy Weir**, published on **May 4, 2021**. It tells the story of **Ryland Grace**, a middle-school science teacher who wakes up alone on a spacecraft with no memory of his mission. He gradually remembers that he is on a desperate mission to save Earth from a microorganism called **astrophage**, which is dimming the Sun. The novel utilizes alternating chapters between present-day events and flashback memories of the mission's planning.\n\nIn terms of critical reception, *Project Hail Mary* has been very well-received. It has an impressive average rating of **4.8 out of 5** across many reader reviews. Critics praise the book for its **optimistic tone**, **scientific rigor**, and the protagonist's compelling voice, as well as a significant relationship within the narrative that many reviewers find heartwarming. It has been compared favorably to Weir's previous work, *The Martian*, and other science fiction classics, garnering recognition as one of the best science fiction novels of 2021.\n\nFor further details, you can check the following sources:\n- [Wikipedia - Project Hail Mary](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Project_Hail_Mary) provides extensive information about the plot and background.\n- Additional reader reviews and ratings can also be helpful to understand the overall sentiments surrounding the book.",
